WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:03.559 --> 00:00:06.119
We are in northern India, in Jharkhand.

00:00:07.400 --> 00:00:09.479
One of the poorest regions in the country.

00:00:11.399 --> 00:00:13.199
Deep in the crevices of this cliff,

00:00:14.279 --> 00:00:17.280
20 or so men and women
are rummaging through the dirt.

00:00:20.559 --> 00:00:22.360
They are mining for mica.

00:00:23.959 --> 00:00:28.159
There are thousands of mines like this
spread across the Jharkhand region.

00:00:29.879 --> 00:00:32.319
They are not run by big corporations.

00:00:34.439 --> 00:00:37.319
Each person collects these stones
for themselves.

00:00:38.599 --> 00:00:45.159
I earn between 100 and 200 rupees,
depending on the market price.

00:00:47.159 --> 00:00:51.080
I have to sell an entire basket
full like this one here.

00:00:51.159 --> 00:00:55.720
Do you know what mica is?

00:00:55.799 --> 00:00:57.279
No, I don't.

00:00:57.360 --> 00:00:59.840
-Do you know what it is used in?
-No.

00:00:59.919 --> 00:01:04.120
-You don't know what it's used for?
-No, I don't.

00:01:06.199 --> 00:01:07.440
For just over a dollar,

00:01:07.519 --> 00:01:10.919
these women are working eight-hour days
under a blazing sun.

00:01:13.480 --> 00:01:17.319
What more can I do? I'm poor.

00:01:17.400 --> 00:01:21.639
I would rather work in the mines
than die of starvation.

00:01:27.559 --> 00:01:30.400
It's not just adults
working in these mines.

00:01:32.000 --> 00:01:35.319
Further down the valley,
we spot a group of children.

00:01:39.800 --> 00:01:42.279
Kids aged between six and nine,

00:01:42.800 --> 00:01:46.839
working in heat that can reach
temperatures of 116 degrees Fahrenheit.

00:01:49.160 --> 00:01:52.239
My name is Gagan Kugar,
I'm eight years old.

00:01:52.400 --> 00:01:54.319
We come together every Sunday.

00:01:54.559 --> 00:01:58.160
What do you do on the other days?

00:01:58.400 --> 00:02:00.919
I go to school to study.

00:02:01.599 --> 00:02:04.919
What time do you get to the mine?

00:02:05.400 --> 00:02:07.360
6:00 am.

00:02:12.000 --> 00:02:14.320
Do you like doing it?

00:02:14.399 --> 00:02:18.119
No, but I can buy school supplies
like books and pens to write with.

00:02:20.160 --> 00:02:22.160
Do you buy anything else?

00:02:22.399 --> 00:02:25.759
Soap and food too.

00:02:34.919 --> 00:02:38.440
This desert landscape
hosts hills that are full of this mineral.

00:02:41.160 --> 00:02:44.399
India is the largest producer
of these shiny strips,

00:02:44.880 --> 00:02:48.399
found by simply reaching down
and collecting them from the ground.

00:02:51.080 --> 00:02:53.520
This raw material
is little known to the public,

00:02:55.559 --> 00:02:58.679
but is in fact integral
for a multitude of products

00:02:58.759 --> 00:03:00.679
that we use in our everyday lives.

00:03:04.759 --> 00:03:06.720
It can be found in car paint,

00:03:09.919 --> 00:03:13.199
as an isolating material
for electronic parts,

00:03:16.600 --> 00:03:20.080
and even as an ingredient
in the cosmetics industry.

00:03:21.600 --> 00:03:26.399
When crushed into a powder, mica is found
in almost every beauty product.

00:03:27.479 --> 00:03:28.520
Mica.

00:03:30.919 --> 00:03:31.960
Mica.

00:03:34.240 --> 00:03:36.440
To find out more
about the product's importance

00:03:36.520 --> 00:03:37.600
in the beauty industry,

00:03:37.679 --> 00:03:41.759
we head to the Carrousel du Louvre
at the Makeup in Paris Trade Fair,

00:03:42.000 --> 00:03:46.119
destined for cosmetic professionals
and experts in this raw material.

00:03:47.039 --> 00:03:50.720
There aren't any stands for Chanel,
Dior, or L'Oréal here,

00:03:51.160 --> 00:03:54.279
as most big brands like these
don't make their own products.

00:03:54.520 --> 00:03:58.399
Instead, outsourcing to manufacturers
who are mostly in Italy.

00:03:59.360 --> 00:04:03.720
Natural mica is an essential ingredient
in makeup such as mascara,

00:04:04.080 --> 00:04:06.520
blush, lipstick, and foundation.

00:04:09.279 --> 00:04:13.839
With this, we're just physically pressing
organic pigments into mica.

00:04:14.360 --> 00:04:18.559
The way most companies formulate,
they typically use mica as the base for,

00:04:18.640 --> 00:04:20.040
let's say, a pressed powder.

00:04:20.200 --> 00:04:25.160
Mica gives the product a shiny quality.

00:04:25.239 --> 00:04:30.880
With its large particles,
you can get a more prominent glow.

00:04:30.959 --> 00:04:37.279
However, when mica is smaller,
it can be used as a base for the product.

00:04:37.359 --> 00:04:43.239
i.e. The product loses its clarity
which in turn intensifies the color.

00:04:45.559 --> 00:04:50.040
When it's applied,
the color comes out a lot brighter.

00:04:50.959 --> 00:04:56.839
Look at this shine,
you can see the glitter in it.

00:04:56.959 --> 00:04:58.720
Basically, there's mica everywhere.

00:04:59.720 --> 00:05:03.600
Yes, you find it in shampoo,
you find it in toothpaste,

00:05:05.480 --> 00:05:09.559
everywhere you have this pearly effect,
you have mica products.

00:05:10.040 --> 00:05:13.760
Manufacturers are well-versed
in their recipes and processes,

00:05:14.519 --> 00:05:17.320
but do they know
where their raw materials are sourced?

00:05:17.399 --> 00:05:20.000
Hello, I am Brando Baranzelli.

00:05:20.079 --> 00:05:22.440
They're aware of the child labor issues

00:05:22.880 --> 00:05:25.440
and claim
that they are very concerned about it.

00:05:25.799 --> 00:05:28.440
We have suppliers
that certify their products' origin.

00:05:28.519 --> 00:05:31.519
It's up to them to take every step
of the process into account.

00:05:31.600 --> 00:05:36.519
We trust our suppliers
and what they tell us.

00:05:36.600 --> 00:05:41.760
We also use regulatory organizations

00:05:41.839 --> 00:05:47.119
that certify our suppliers
don't use child labor.

00:05:47.200 --> 00:05:50.839
We only use mica
for which we know the source,

00:05:50.920 --> 00:05:55.160
and if the supplier is part of an official
list of multinational companies,

00:05:55.239 --> 00:05:58.839
because these companies
are well aware of this problem

00:05:58.920 --> 00:06:01.040
and are constantly tackling it.

00:06:01.119 --> 00:06:05.839
They draw up lists of suppliers
that are socially responsible

00:06:05.920 --> 00:06:10.559
and respect the correct ethical standards.

00:06:14.720 --> 00:06:17.440
However, what is the real story
behind these claims?

00:06:18.839 --> 00:06:21.000
Mica can be found all over the world.

00:06:22.880 --> 00:06:26.000
The major producers
are the US, South Korea,

00:06:26.640 --> 00:06:30.799
Brazil, Canada, China,
and of course, India.

00:06:31.519 --> 00:06:34.040
According to the official organisation
Eurostat,

00:06:34.559 --> 00:06:38.279
India represents 30%
of all mica imported into Europe.

00:06:39.519 --> 00:06:43.160
Officially, mica produced in India
comes from Rajasthan.

00:06:43.959 --> 00:06:45.239
However, in reality,

00:06:45.720 --> 00:06:50.239
most of the deposits are found
in the states of Jharkhand and Bihar,

00:06:50.720 --> 00:06:54.399
a region where mica mining
happens illegally and in secret.

00:06:55.880 --> 00:06:57.839
Almost 90% of mica.

00:07:03.040 --> 00:07:05.200
Can we really be sure
of the conditions

00:07:05.279 --> 00:07:08.119
in which this essential mineral
for our skin is extracted?

00:07:11.119 --> 00:07:12.480
We are back in Jharkhand.

00:07:13.600 --> 00:07:16.279
These wild valleys,
which spread for miles,

00:07:16.720 --> 00:07:20.880
were declared a natural reserve
by the state in the 1990s.

00:07:21.760 --> 00:07:25.640
In order to protect them,
the authorities banned all mica mining.

00:07:28.279 --> 00:07:33.239
However, this drone footage shows
that there are huge numbers of mines here.

00:07:35.519 --> 00:07:36.839
These surface craters

00:07:37.320 --> 00:07:41.160
testify to the sheer amount of mining
that's been carried out by villagers,

00:07:41.359 --> 00:07:44.399
even in areas
that are very difficult to access.

00:07:47.839 --> 00:07:50.839
Some miners are using dynamite
to open up the mountains,

00:07:51.799 --> 00:07:54.920
while others use more rudimentary methods.

00:07:57.679 --> 00:08:01.959
In order to understand why this mining
has taken place for over 40 years,

00:08:02.160 --> 00:08:04.079
despite the bans in place,

00:08:05.079 --> 00:08:07.399
we decided to get in touch
with the miners.

00:08:08.399 --> 00:08:10.279
It was hard to spot them in the field.

00:08:12.559 --> 00:08:15.000
After two days of searching,
we met a family.

00:08:20.720 --> 00:08:22.640
Anil is 25 years old.

00:08:23.399 --> 00:08:26.880
Every day, he comes here to mine mica
with his wife and children.

00:08:29.679 --> 00:08:32.640
Mica is the only option for us.

00:08:32.719 --> 00:08:37.359
We have all come here to work
and earn around 300 to 400 rupees

00:08:37.440 --> 00:08:41.359
so we can buy rice and feed ourselves.

00:08:43.000 --> 00:08:47.760
I want them to study,
to do something with their lives.

00:08:48.799 --> 00:08:53.159
I want them to have a good job.

00:08:55.479 --> 00:08:57.400
Anil wasn't always a miner.

00:08:57.719 --> 00:09:00.599
Just two years ago,
he was working as a farmer.

00:09:01.280 --> 00:09:05.119
He lives in this village,
located at the foot of the mines,

00:09:05.400 --> 00:09:07.719
with a population of around 60 people.

00:09:08.479 --> 00:09:12.599
There is no running water or electricity
despite the brand-new poles.

00:09:16.119 --> 00:09:18.479
The family's livelihood
used to be farming.

00:09:19.359 --> 00:09:22.239
However, due to drought
and climate change,

00:09:22.760 --> 00:09:24.640
most of the land is now barren.

00:09:26.200 --> 00:09:30.159
This is my land, here, all of this.

00:09:31.039 --> 00:09:33.520
Can you still farm on this land?

00:09:33.760 --> 00:09:34.960
No, of course not.

00:09:35.039 --> 00:09:38.000
If there is no rain then nothing can grow.

00:09:38.080 --> 00:09:39.760
It's bone dry.

00:09:40.679 --> 00:09:44.599
The extraction of mica
is now an essential source of revenue

00:09:44.679 --> 00:09:47.719
for more than 90%
of Jharkhand's population.

00:09:49.799 --> 00:09:53.359
Miners are willing to take huge risks
to get their hands on it.

00:09:55.119 --> 00:09:56.679
Over-mined on the surface,

00:09:57.919 --> 00:10:01.559
they have to go deeper and deeper
in order to find this precious mineral.

00:10:03.000 --> 00:10:06.479
The sound of mining work
near a well caught our attention.

00:10:07.799 --> 00:10:10.799
[Foreign spoken audio]

00:10:21.799 --> 00:10:24.159
Don't worry, we're not police.

00:10:24.239 --> 00:10:25.359
Okay, no problem.

00:10:29.919 --> 00:10:32.760
-What is your name?
-Karan Singh.

00:10:33.159 --> 00:10:35.919
How do you deal with working down there?

00:10:36.200 --> 00:10:41.119
When you're hungry,
you're not afraid to go down.

00:10:41.200 --> 00:10:43.760
Yes, it's dangerous work,
but what else can you do?

00:10:44.400 --> 00:10:48.320
I need to eat,
I don't really have a choice.

00:10:48.400 --> 00:10:51.320
I haven't studied a lot

00:10:51.599 --> 00:10:54.119
and I don't get any help
from the government.

00:10:56.679 --> 00:11:00.119
Karan is 35 years old
and has two children.

00:11:00.840 --> 00:11:03.599
He allows us to follow him
into the tunnel he has built.

00:11:06.159 --> 00:11:09.640
Every month,
around 12 miners die in the region

00:11:10.000 --> 00:11:12.520
because of these dangerous
underground quarries.

00:11:15.080 --> 00:11:19.479
Almost 50 feet underground,
their supply is running low.

00:11:20.479 --> 00:11:22.520
It's around 113 degrees,

00:11:22.919 --> 00:11:25.559
and there's nothing in place
to hold up the structure.

00:11:26.000 --> 00:11:27.640
It could collapse at any moment.

00:11:37.359 --> 00:11:38.919
Karan and his friend Ravi

00:11:39.000 --> 00:11:41.359
spend eight hours a day
in the darkness here.

00:11:44.440 --> 00:11:47.400
This ordeal brings them
around 300 rupees a day.

00:11:47.599 --> 00:11:51.080
The equivalent of 2.75 dollars.

00:11:52.400 --> 00:11:54.200
I've worked here for four months.

00:11:54.280 --> 00:11:56.960
We've had a lot of people
working here in the past.

00:11:57.039 --> 00:11:59.520
Our ancestors worked here
40 to 50 years ago.

00:12:00.159 --> 00:12:04.119
Are you aware that people die
due to these mines collapsing?

00:12:04.200 --> 00:12:06.679
I am scared for my life
like anyone would be,

00:12:06.760 --> 00:12:08.039
but what else can I do?

00:12:08.599 --> 00:12:14.359
There aren't too many accidents here.

00:12:15.000 --> 00:12:17.000
If God so chooses, it will happen,

00:12:17.080 --> 00:12:20.239
but for now,
there haven't been any disasters here.

00:12:36.479 --> 00:12:38.280
Mica can be found on the surface

00:12:38.359 --> 00:12:41.119
but higher quantities
can be found underground.

00:12:41.400 --> 00:12:45.000
Here, for example, there are large stones,

00:12:45.159 --> 00:12:48.559
whereas up here there isn't any mica,

00:12:48.640 --> 00:12:50.840
so we haven't touched it.

00:12:51.559 --> 00:12:55.520
There's a lot over there
so we head that way.

00:12:56.000 --> 00:12:59.119
It's good quality here too.

00:12:59.200 --> 00:13:02.039
Does it not worry you
that what you're doing is illegal?

00:13:02.200 --> 00:13:04.719
The police came around four
or five months ago.

00:13:05.359 --> 00:13:10.320
They said that it's illegal
and that we have to stop.

00:13:10.679 --> 00:13:13.719
They even tried to scare us sometimes,

00:13:13.799 --> 00:13:17.919
but how are we going to feed ourselves
if we don't come here?

00:13:18.080 --> 00:13:20.960
They said they'll do everything
in their power to arrest us

00:13:21.039 --> 00:13:22.400
and take us to the station.

00:13:22.799 --> 00:13:24.440
They've arrested us at times

00:13:24.520 --> 00:13:27.719
but then let us go afterward
because they know we're poor.

00:13:27.960 --> 00:13:33.599
Sometimes they take a bit of money
from us, 1,000 rupees max.

00:13:35.599 --> 00:13:38.080
The mountain however is less forgiving.

00:13:42.760 --> 00:13:46.960
Karan plays down the danger,
but people have died in his own village.

00:13:52.760 --> 00:13:54.840
These two miners live in Tisri,

00:13:56.119 --> 00:14:00.919
a town with a population of around 4,000
that is surrounded by mining deposits.

00:14:01.760 --> 00:14:03.960
Mining is the main source of income here.

00:14:11.080 --> 00:14:13.239
Three years ago, disaster hit.

00:14:14.919 --> 00:14:17.080
This woman lost her husband to the mines.

00:14:18.000 --> 00:14:19.359
She has four children.

00:14:24.679 --> 00:14:27.119
Sit down and eat.

00:14:32.880 --> 00:14:34.840
Like most of the Jharkhand villagers,

00:14:35.479 --> 00:14:36.840
she cannot read or write.

00:14:40.000 --> 00:14:41.840
My name is Anita Devi.

00:14:42.080 --> 00:14:45.719
I don't know how old I am,
my parents don't remember.

00:14:47.359 --> 00:14:51.320
Can you tell us about your husband?

00:14:53.359 --> 00:14:55.919
My husband left to work in the mines,

00:14:56.200 --> 00:15:00.039
he went deep into the ground

00:15:00.200 --> 00:15:03.719
and was buried alive after a landslide.

00:15:05.000 --> 00:15:09.719
-Did others die?
-Yes, three others.

00:15:18.119 --> 00:15:22.840
Since her husband died,
Anita is the only provider for her family.

00:15:26.119 --> 00:15:30.719
Every day, she walks over a mile
under the hot sun on rocky paths

00:15:31.200 --> 00:15:33.359
before reaching the summit
of this mountain.

00:15:37.359 --> 00:15:40.640
When they aren't at school,
her children come with her to work.

00:15:41.280 --> 00:15:43.520
The youngest is just four years old.

00:15:46.000 --> 00:15:50.159
The children help me
to collect the small rocks.

00:15:51.159 --> 00:15:54.520
We crush and collect the rock debris

00:15:54.799 --> 00:15:59.320
that is on the surface.

00:16:00.599 --> 00:16:02.760
Therefore, I earn less.

00:16:08.159 --> 00:16:12.559
Mommy something has got into my foot.

00:16:13.200 --> 00:16:16.159
Show me, show me.

00:16:17.400 --> 00:16:22.440
Show me, otherwise, I'll get annoyed!

00:16:26.359 --> 00:16:29.919
This is my daily ordeal,
working in the heat.

00:16:30.400 --> 00:16:33.000
I can deal with hunger
but not my children.

00:16:33.080 --> 00:16:34.559
I won't let them starve.

00:16:35.200 --> 00:16:38.559
I have to work
as I don't have any land to farm.

00:16:40.799 --> 00:16:41.880
After three hours,

00:16:41.960 --> 00:16:43.799
Anita and her children
have collected enough

00:16:43.880 --> 00:16:45.440
to feed themselves for a day.

00:16:48.239 --> 00:16:53.280
It's a poor man's work,
but many big businesses rely on it.

00:16:58.679 --> 00:17:00.320
Back with Karan and Ravi.

00:17:03.280 --> 00:17:07.160
We're trying to understand
where their mica goes once it's sold.

00:17:07.880 --> 00:17:09.839
Is it destined for the European market?

00:17:10.000 --> 00:17:13.239
Where does the mica go
once you have collected it?

00:17:14.160 --> 00:17:16.920
To the city of Giridih.

00:17:17.000 --> 00:17:18.920
Who do you give it to?

00:17:19.599 --> 00:17:24.719
Someone who comes to get it in Thana,
around four miles from the main road.

00:17:25.400 --> 00:17:27.160
Are these people wholesalers over there?

00:17:27.239 --> 00:17:31.319
Yes, the wholesalers come there to buy it.

00:17:31.400 --> 00:17:33.760
Does it go to Giridih only after that?

00:17:34.599 --> 00:17:39.280
Yes, they transport it there
because they have a license.

00:17:39.359 --> 00:17:43.439
What sort of license?
You didn't know it was illegal?

00:17:44.800 --> 00:17:50.119
Yes, you need a license
to be able to sell it.

00:17:50.880 --> 00:17:53.280
Can we go and meet them?

00:17:53.359 --> 00:17:56.560
Sure, if you go there
they'll explain everything,

00:17:56.640 --> 00:17:59.599
You will see outside there
are big factories

00:17:59.680 --> 00:18:03.520
next to the police station,
it's written in big letters.

00:18:06.760 --> 00:18:10.680
We realized that despite this product
being illegally sourced,

00:18:11.520 --> 00:18:15.319
it can be easily exchanged on the market
through several intermediaries.

00:18:18.920 --> 00:18:20.239
At the end of each day,

00:18:21.040 --> 00:18:25.040
the villagers take what they've collected
towards the valley to collection points

00:18:25.359 --> 00:18:27.239
where the minerals are sold by weight.

00:18:34.760 --> 00:18:38.439
Put it on here.

00:18:41.359 --> 00:18:44.359
These small retailers
supply the production line

00:18:46.359 --> 00:18:48.880
and sell mica to the local wholesalers.

00:18:56.280 --> 00:18:58.680
The local residents direct me
to the wholesalers

00:18:59.199 --> 00:19:01.160
that will eventually buy their product.

00:19:02.839 --> 00:19:05.040
We head to the center of town
to meet them.

00:19:06.199 --> 00:19:07.680
There were more than a dozen of them,

00:19:07.760 --> 00:19:10.760
as mica production
is the town's only industry.

00:19:15.400 --> 00:19:17.800
At first, they refused to be filmed.

00:19:19.359 --> 00:19:21.760
Eventually, one of the wholesalers

00:19:21.839 --> 00:19:24.520
agreed to respond
to our questions off-camera.

00:19:25.560 --> 00:19:28.119
We filmed the following scenes
with a hidden camera.

00:19:33.359 --> 00:19:35.560
Where does the mica come from?

00:19:36.160 --> 00:19:39.319
The mica comes from the mines.

00:19:40.079 --> 00:19:42.439
Is it the small retailers
that bring it to you?

00:19:42.520 --> 00:19:43.719
Yes.

00:19:43.800 --> 00:19:47.880
The wholesaler admits that the mica
is sourced from illegal mines.

00:19:48.400 --> 00:19:51.439
However, as soon as we suggest
that it comes from child labor,

00:19:51.560 --> 00:19:52.599
he shuts down.

00:19:53.599 --> 00:19:57.640
We'd like to ask you
about children working in the mine.

00:19:58.760 --> 00:20:02.319
Children don't work in the mica mines.

00:20:03.599 --> 00:20:07.719
It's false information.

00:20:11.199 --> 00:20:16.199
The children bring food to their parents

00:20:16.280 --> 00:20:19.239
when they are working,

00:20:21.239 --> 00:20:27.439
and the media takes photos of it.

00:20:31.560 --> 00:20:35.040
-Therefore, children don't work there?
-No.

00:20:35.199 --> 00:20:38.839
Do you export too?

00:20:39.199 --> 00:20:40.719
No, we sell to the exporters.

00:20:40.959 --> 00:20:46.920
It goes to Mumbai, China, Germany…

00:20:47.479 --> 00:20:50.520
Who buys it in Germany?

00:20:50.599 --> 00:20:52.920
Merck.

00:20:53.839 --> 00:20:57.439
One of the main buyers of the mica
that's produced in the region is,

00:20:57.520 --> 00:21:01.000
according to this man,
the German group Merck.

00:21:04.280 --> 00:21:07.160
Merck is one of the largest corporations
in Germany.

00:21:09.760 --> 00:21:11.520
Founded in 1668,

00:21:12.040 --> 00:21:15.239
this multinational earns
over 16 billion dollars

00:21:15.319 --> 00:21:18.520
in the chemical, cosmetics,
and pharmaceutical industries.

00:21:18.599 --> 00:21:21.599
Merck has the oldest chemical
and pharmaceutical company,

00:21:21.920 --> 00:21:26.079
bundles 350 years of expertise
from healthcare, life science,

00:21:26.199 --> 00:21:27.640
and performance materials,

00:21:27.800 --> 00:21:31.040
and translates it
into cosmetic ingredient development.

00:21:31.719 --> 00:21:34.000
We call this translational cosmetics.

00:21:34.079 --> 00:21:36.920
The European leader
in supplying raw materials

00:21:37.000 --> 00:21:38.439
to the cosmetics industry.

00:21:40.079 --> 00:21:43.439
Subsidiaries such as the Colorona
and Timiron Group

00:21:44.000 --> 00:21:46.000
are the main mica pigment suppliers

00:21:46.079 --> 00:21:50.359
to big brands
such as L'Oréal, Chanel, and Girling.

00:21:50.439 --> 00:21:53.160
This is the Merck way
to innovate in beauty.

00:21:56.560 --> 00:21:58.079
At this beauty trade fair,

00:21:58.160 --> 00:22:00.760
we approach the representatives
of the German company

00:22:00.959 --> 00:22:02.920
to question them on their supply chain.

00:22:04.599 --> 00:22:06.000
It's a sensitive subject,

00:22:06.680 --> 00:22:09.079
so we chose not to warn them
that we were coming.

00:22:10.560 --> 00:22:13.560
Hello, nice to meet you,
I'm Brando, Special Report.

00:22:14.000 --> 00:22:17.560
We're making a film
about the cosmetics market and mica,

00:22:18.199 --> 00:22:22.959
and we're visiting different stands
to talk to different producers.

00:22:23.199 --> 00:22:25.520
Will you be able to answer
some of our questions?

00:22:25.599 --> 00:22:28.119
-No one from communications is here.
-Sorry?

00:22:28.199 --> 00:22:31.119
We don't have anyone from communications,
did you schedule this interview?

00:22:31.199 --> 00:22:36.839
-No.
-They're in Germany and also on vacation.

00:22:36.959 --> 00:22:39.119
You should have made
an appointment beforehand.

00:22:39.199 --> 00:22:41.680
However, we haven't made an appointment
with the other stands.

00:22:41.760 --> 00:22:44.680
We just asked people a few questions
and they answered them.

00:22:44.760 --> 00:22:47.560
Well, we don't work like that.

00:22:49.160 --> 00:22:51.800
The stand manager
suggests we write an email

00:22:51.880 --> 00:22:53.359
to her colleagues in Germany.

00:22:54.920 --> 00:22:56.319
We did this the next day.

00:22:57.520 --> 00:23:01.400
The company declined our offer
of an interview without giving any reason.

00:23:02.239 --> 00:23:06.599
"Unfortunately,
I cannot offer you an appointment"

00:23:06.680 --> 00:23:08.880
"for a personal interview."

00:23:08.959 --> 00:23:13.880
Whilst waiting, they suggested we read
their corporate responsibility information

00:23:14.239 --> 00:23:15.760
accessible on their website.

00:23:16.800 --> 00:23:20.439
It claims a zero-tolerance policy
for child labor.

00:23:20.520 --> 00:23:23.719
"We have completely reorganized
our supply chain"

00:23:23.800 --> 00:23:27.439
"and now source the raw material
exclusively from qualified mines."

00:23:27.959 --> 00:23:32.839
"The control of relevant documentation,
worker's ages, working hours and wages,"

00:23:32.920 --> 00:23:37.400
"as well as compliance with environmental,
safety, and health standards."

00:23:38.199 --> 00:23:42.199
"By means of audits, we strictly monitor
the compliant behavior of our partners,"

00:23:42.280 --> 00:23:45.280
"who've agreed to adhere to the principles
of our Human Rights Charter"

00:23:45.359 --> 00:23:48.280
"as well as the requirements
of our Responsible Sourcing Principles."

00:23:48.359 --> 00:23:49.800
To confirm these statements,

00:23:50.520 --> 00:23:54.839
we headed back to India,
to Koderma, a city in northern Jharkhand.

00:23:55.880 --> 00:24:00.880
This town, with a population of 24,000,
is the hub of the mica industry,

00:24:01.199 --> 00:24:03.719
containing the majority
of the export businesses

00:24:04.040 --> 00:24:05.400
and treatment facilities.

00:24:11.000 --> 00:24:14.760
Hello? Who is it?

00:24:21.400 --> 00:24:26.280
Shaitan is 25 years old
and he's one of the exporters in town.

00:24:28.680 --> 00:24:32.560
When I introduce myself as a journalist,
he agrees to show me his warehouses

00:24:32.920 --> 00:24:35.439
and respond to questions
about child labor.

00:24:39.800 --> 00:24:43.319
Hassan, go and get some material.

00:24:47.160 --> 00:24:50.239
He has to have the material ready here
next to the machine.

00:24:50.319 --> 00:24:53.000
His business has around 50 employees.

00:24:58.359 --> 00:25:03.079
The process involves
screening the raw materials.

00:25:04.760 --> 00:25:07.319
They are placed in the screener,

00:25:10.520 --> 00:25:15.520
where all the sand particles
and impurities are removed.

00:25:17.880 --> 00:25:22.680
The resulting material
will be clean and free of sand.

00:25:27.400 --> 00:25:29.319
Sorted, ground, and filtered,

00:25:29.920 --> 00:25:32.599
the crystals
are then refined one final time

00:25:32.680 --> 00:25:34.560
before becoming the final product.

00:25:35.760 --> 00:25:38.160
These are impurity-free mica flakes.

00:25:38.880 --> 00:25:42.920
It is widely used in pigments
and cosmetic industries.

00:25:43.319 --> 00:25:45.280
Impurity-free mica flakes.

00:25:48.239 --> 00:25:52.160
These precious mica flakes are wrapped
and then exported to Europe,

00:25:52.520 --> 00:25:55.839
and sold at around 550 dollars per ton.

00:25:57.319 --> 00:25:59.119
Listening to the young entrepreneur,

00:25:59.239 --> 00:26:01.760
there's a good reason
his mica isn't sourced

00:26:01.839 --> 00:26:03.839
from mines that use child labor.

00:26:05.400 --> 00:26:07.199
It comes from Rajasthan,

00:26:07.479 --> 00:26:11.160
where extraction is legal
and controlled by the authorities.

00:26:16.280 --> 00:26:21.319
This is a lorry from Rajasthan
that comes from the legal mica mines

00:26:21.760 --> 00:26:23.880
and unloads at our factory.

00:26:26.959 --> 00:26:31.560
There, all the mica mines
are legally run by their owners.

00:26:34.400 --> 00:26:39.000
According to NGOs, three-quarters
of the country's mica deposits

00:26:39.079 --> 00:26:44.239
aren't situated in Rajasthan,
but rather around Koderma in Jharkhand.

00:26:47.119 --> 00:26:49.119
When working on the Merck investigation,

00:26:50.280 --> 00:26:53.560
we found a database
that records mica exports

00:26:53.640 --> 00:26:55.040
from the port in Kolkata.

00:26:58.760 --> 00:27:02.359
We saw that Merck gets several containers
a week delivered to Germany

00:27:03.319 --> 00:27:06.479
and is supplied
by two exporters based in Koderma.

00:27:08.079 --> 00:27:09.119
Ramdew Modi

00:27:11.000 --> 00:27:12.400
and Pachisia and Company.

00:27:13.599 --> 00:27:15.640
Both are businesses that we know well.

00:27:18.599 --> 00:27:21.520
When we were conducting
our investigation in the villages,

00:27:22.239 --> 00:27:24.599
the wholesaler confirmed
that these businesses

00:27:24.680 --> 00:27:26.280
work with illegal mines.

00:27:27.160 --> 00:27:29.959
Do you export too?

00:27:30.040 --> 00:27:32.319
No, we sell to the exporters.

00:27:32.400 --> 00:27:34.719
-To Ramdew Modi too?
-Yes, exactly.

00:27:34.880 --> 00:27:36.160
Pachisia too?

00:27:36.599 --> 00:27:37.920
Pachisia… Yes.

00:27:38.000 --> 00:27:41.719
I supply them too,
they are in charge of exporting it.

00:27:43.239 --> 00:27:47.280
We managed to find these two suppliers
to Merck on the outskirts of Koderma.

00:27:47.680 --> 00:27:49.760
They're located right next to one another.

00:27:50.160 --> 00:27:52.520
We pay them a visit
with our hidden cameras.

00:27:59.680 --> 00:28:01.319
As soon as we arrive at Pachisia,

00:28:02.280 --> 00:28:05.000
all the workers scurry away
in a matter of seconds.

00:28:11.119 --> 00:28:12.839
Only one man welcomes us.

00:28:13.359 --> 00:28:14.920
A man who seems to be the boss.

00:28:15.040 --> 00:28:16.119
-Brando?
-Yes.

00:28:17.439 --> 00:28:18.959
Posing as a potential buyer,

00:28:19.560 --> 00:28:22.520
I try to find out more
about his suppliers and clients,

00:28:23.119 --> 00:28:25.079
but the man quickly becomes suspicious.

00:28:26.880 --> 00:28:29.400
Actually, at the moment,

00:28:30.839 --> 00:28:36.160
I'm very sorry that I am unable
to discuss any business topics

00:28:36.319 --> 00:28:38.760
without my father's permission

00:28:38.920 --> 00:28:40.920
because he is the senior person.

00:28:41.079 --> 00:28:42.119
-Your father?
-Yes.

00:28:44.680 --> 00:28:45.839
We hit a brick wall.

00:28:47.839 --> 00:28:49.839
After, we head to Ramdew Modi.

00:28:52.199 --> 00:28:53.719
We're welcomed by the foremen,

00:28:53.800 --> 00:28:56.760
and the boss says over the phone
that he can't see us.

00:29:01.839 --> 00:29:06.439
Disappointed, we are getting ready
to leave when we spot another factory

00:29:06.520 --> 00:29:08.800
just 100 feet away from the first two.

00:29:11.599 --> 00:29:16.239
This time, the boss is there
and he welcomes us with open arms.

00:29:17.199 --> 00:29:20.280
He knows his neighbors well
and works with them often.

00:29:21.079 --> 00:29:26.199
Still posing as a potential buyer,
I ask him about Ramdew Modi and Pachisia.

00:29:26.680 --> 00:29:30.920
They've been doing that for a long time,
their mica basically goes to Merck.

00:29:31.160 --> 00:29:33.719
Merck in Germany.

00:29:35.640 --> 00:29:37.079
The man is happy to chat

00:29:37.680 --> 00:29:40.640
and reveals the secrets
about trade with foreign countries.

00:29:41.280 --> 00:29:44.079
-Are they allowed to export?
-Yes, they've got an export license.

00:29:44.160 --> 00:29:46.920
They don't have any mining operations,

00:29:47.599 --> 00:29:50.520
but they manage
to get the documents anyway.

00:29:50.599 --> 00:29:53.400
Their merchandise comes from here.
It's not legal at all.

00:29:53.599 --> 00:29:55.160
It's not legal at all.

00:29:56.199 --> 00:30:01.119
You can get licenses
from Rajasthan or Belwahra

00:30:01.199 --> 00:30:04.319
because there is mica there.

00:30:04.400 --> 00:30:10.319
To appear above board,
the exporters use licenses from there.

00:30:12.160 --> 00:30:15.160
While their mica
comes from illegal mines in Jharkhand,

00:30:15.839 --> 00:30:19.439
the trick for exporters
is to buy a license from Rajasthan,

00:30:19.959 --> 00:30:21.760
to make their businesses legitimate,

00:30:21.959 --> 00:30:25.000
and to export their products
with the correct paperwork.

00:30:27.880 --> 00:30:30.079
The man then introduces us
to his colleague.

00:30:34.760 --> 00:30:37.520
He informs us that it is also possible

00:30:37.599 --> 00:30:41.719
for import businesses
to get a certificate of ethical conduct

00:30:41.800 --> 00:30:43.160
regarding child labor.

00:30:43.719 --> 00:30:45.439
All you have to do is pay.

00:30:49.160 --> 00:30:51.920
If the buyer wants a certificate,
how can you do this?

00:30:52.000 --> 00:30:55.920
You can get one with the business's name.

00:30:56.000 --> 00:30:59.439
We find the paper,
we can do everything without any problems.

00:30:59.920 --> 00:31:01.839
Therefore, it's feasible?

00:31:01.920 --> 00:31:06.160
Yes, we take care of everything.

00:31:06.400 --> 00:31:10.520
However, if you don't get these papers,
it will cost you a lot.

00:31:11.560 --> 00:31:13.760
The administrative part is expensive.

00:31:13.839 --> 00:31:15.119
How much?

00:31:15.199 --> 00:31:16.560
Two or 2.5 rupees per kilo.

00:31:17.880 --> 00:31:19.959
No matter where the mica is from,

00:31:20.400 --> 00:31:24.800
it's easy to get papers that prove
it hasn't been produced by child labor.

00:31:27.239 --> 00:31:29.239
Here is what the certificates look like.

00:31:30.160 --> 00:31:31.520
This particular copy

00:31:31.680 --> 00:31:35.280
comes from an Indian company
that provides international certification.

00:31:36.319 --> 00:31:39.839
It ensures that the mica
has never been touched by a child's hands.

00:31:40.719 --> 00:31:42.520
According to this Indian exporter,

00:31:43.079 --> 00:31:47.599
these papers are a mandatory requirement
for international groups like Merck.

00:31:51.680 --> 00:31:54.680
There's a phrase we use here:

00:31:54.760 --> 00:31:59.079
"Does that mean that people
who don't own cows can't drink milk?"

00:31:59.160 --> 00:32:01.280
In the same way,
if you aren't above board,

00:32:01.359 --> 00:32:04.760
is it therefore impossible
to have the right paperwork?

00:32:04.839 --> 00:32:06.560
That's how the world works.

00:32:06.959 --> 00:32:11.000
Of course, large corporations like Merck
conduct their own inspections.

00:32:11.920 --> 00:32:13.520
However, according to this boss,

00:32:14.000 --> 00:32:16.760
exporters also have tricks
to get around this.

00:32:17.599 --> 00:32:22.040
When Merck inspectors come,
for example when Mr. X came here,

00:32:23.160 --> 00:32:26.920
he asked me to bring him
to the mines for a visit.

00:32:28.359 --> 00:32:32.359
Were there children working in the mines?

00:32:33.160 --> 00:32:36.719
Yes, there are children
working in the mines too

00:32:36.800 --> 00:32:39.959
but on the day of the inspection,
there wasn't a child in sight.

00:32:40.040 --> 00:32:41.239
No women or children.

00:32:41.760 --> 00:32:43.079
How can we be sure

00:32:43.359 --> 00:32:45.719
that the mica
imported by this German group

00:32:45.800 --> 00:32:48.040
has never passed through a child's hands?

00:32:50.280 --> 00:32:51.839
Upon my return to Paris,

00:32:52.319 --> 00:32:55.239
I wanted to confront the Merck Group
with my investigation.

00:32:55.760 --> 00:32:58.000
I sent an email
to the communications department

00:32:58.079 --> 00:33:00.439
recounting the discoveries
I had made in India

00:33:01.119 --> 00:33:03.040
during our investigation in Koderma.

00:33:03.319 --> 00:33:07.239
We spoke with some of their partners
who told us that both Ramdew and Pachisia,

00:33:07.439 --> 00:33:08.560
like all other exporters,

00:33:08.640 --> 00:33:10.920
provide themselves
with mica collectors in Jharkhand,

00:33:11.000 --> 00:33:14.199
whose mica comes from illegal mines
involving child labor.

00:33:14.640 --> 00:33:16.239
In their response, the business sent us

00:33:16.319 --> 00:33:19.359
their corporate responsibility information
again, assuring us,

00:33:19.560 --> 00:33:21.239
"Based on our available information,"

00:33:21.319 --> 00:33:24.000
"your statement that our suppliers
would source third-party mica"

00:33:24.079 --> 00:33:27.239
"from illegal mines
involving child labor is incorrect."

00:33:30.040 --> 00:33:33.920
Continuing our research,
we found a Paris-based association,

00:33:34.199 --> 00:33:36.000
the Responsible Mica Initiative.

00:33:36.560 --> 00:33:39.560
An organization
that seeks to eradicate child labor

00:33:39.680 --> 00:33:41.199
in the Indian mica mines.

00:33:43.280 --> 00:33:45.599
It states that it lobbies
the Indian authorities

00:33:45.680 --> 00:33:49.800
and carries out social action
in nearly 80 villages across Jharkhand.

00:33:53.319 --> 00:33:58.560
Among the 50 or so sponsors
are Merck, L'Oréal, Chanel,

00:33:59.079 --> 00:34:00.239
and Yves Rocher.

00:34:03.040 --> 00:34:05.760
The manager for France
has agreed to meet with us.

00:34:11.800 --> 00:34:14.560
-Hello, nice to meet you.
-Nice to meet you.

00:34:15.320 --> 00:34:16.360
At their offices,

00:34:16.719 --> 00:34:20.159
we show her images
that we filmed in the mines in India.

00:34:35.360 --> 00:34:38.879
It's unbearable to watch this,
that's why we need to act and act now.

00:34:38.959 --> 00:34:40.560
This is why our organization was founded

00:34:40.639 --> 00:34:43.280
and why we have fixed
extremely ambitious objectives,

00:34:43.360 --> 00:34:46.080
aiming to eradicate child labor by 2022.

00:34:46.159 --> 00:34:49.120
Fanny Freeman is aware
that child labor is still an issue,

00:34:49.199 --> 00:34:51.760
but assured us
that it's out of the question

00:34:51.840 --> 00:34:53.520
for brands to leave the region.

00:34:53.760 --> 00:34:56.959
If these businesses
decided to stop buying mica from India,

00:34:57.760 --> 00:35:00.040
in the end,
it's the families that would suffer

00:35:00.120 --> 00:35:01.479
from losing their own income,

00:35:01.560 --> 00:35:06.520
so this is why I say it is brave to stay,
to know there is a problem,

00:35:06.879 --> 00:35:08.600
but to say to ourselves: "We're staying,"

00:35:08.679 --> 00:35:11.879
"we're aware and we're doing everything
in our power to solve it".

00:35:12.199 --> 00:35:14.040
Mica is their only source of revenue.

00:35:14.120 --> 00:35:18.320
If all of the businesses left India
and sourced elsewhere,

00:35:18.399 --> 00:35:22.919
it would have disastrous social
and economic consequences.

00:35:26.320 --> 00:35:29.919
Towards the end of our investigation,
we made one last discovery.

00:35:34.199 --> 00:35:36.360
We're back in the mining region of Tisri.

00:35:39.399 --> 00:35:42.000
Over recent years
of excessive exploitation,

00:35:42.600 --> 00:35:45.439
mining has had an impact
on the health of the population.

00:35:49.679 --> 00:35:50.719
The village hospital

00:35:50.800 --> 00:35:54.120
has a room dedicated to people
suffering from tuberculosis.

00:35:59.199 --> 00:36:01.360
Bishupal is waiting for his appointment.

00:36:04.000 --> 00:36:06.520
He has spent ten years
working in the mica mines.

00:36:07.560 --> 00:36:08.840
Bishupal, you can go in.

00:36:10.080 --> 00:36:13.760
For the past month, he's been suffering
with respiratory problems.

00:36:16.199 --> 00:36:18.159
-What is the problem?
-I have a cough.

00:36:18.679 --> 00:36:21.199
-For how long?
-A month.

00:36:21.280 --> 00:36:22.360
Come here.

00:36:22.800 --> 00:36:24.639
The doctor in this makeshift hospital

00:36:25.040 --> 00:36:26.840
sees a hundred or so patients a day.

00:36:27.000 --> 00:36:29.159
Try to cough. Cough, cough, cough…

00:36:41.919 --> 00:36:44.600
Around 60% of them
are suffering from coughs.

00:36:45.399 --> 00:36:46.800
Do these tests and begin treatment.

00:36:46.879 --> 00:36:49.520
Return with the test results,
and I'll prescribe other medication,

00:36:49.600 --> 00:36:50.879
depending on the results.

00:36:53.439 --> 00:36:58.439
Many people who work in these mining
areas are exposed to dust particles,

00:36:58.560 --> 00:37:03.719
which can lead
to problems like tuberculosis,

00:37:03.800 --> 00:37:07.040
especially when the exposure is prolonged.

00:37:07.120 --> 00:37:10.239
There's a chance that more than 80
to 90% of the workers

00:37:10.320 --> 00:37:12.280
may face health issues due to the dust.

00:37:12.639 --> 00:37:16.120
The complications can affect
not only those working in the mines

00:37:16.199 --> 00:37:18.280
but also anyone
living in this environment,

00:37:18.360 --> 00:37:21.479
as they too may be affected
by the same problems.

00:37:24.080 --> 00:37:27.439
Take one tablet
every evening after dinner.

00:37:32.399 --> 00:37:34.159
Do these non-regulated mines

00:37:34.239 --> 00:37:37.239
risk having an impact
on the health of an entire generation?

00:37:38.280 --> 00:37:42.520
We can't really say, but these hospitals
located in mining regions

00:37:43.199 --> 00:37:47.159
see a higher rate of pulmonary illnesses
than anywhere else in India.

00:37:51.520 --> 00:37:54.120
However, local residents
aren't aware of this,

00:37:54.800 --> 00:37:57.040
and children are particularly at risk.

00:38:13.399 --> 00:38:18.320
An association from Koderma is campaigning
to alert the miners in the villages.

00:38:18.919 --> 00:38:22.159
We talk with the villagers,
advising them not to work in the mines

00:38:22.560 --> 00:38:26.760
because it has a very bad impact
on their health.

00:38:27.399 --> 00:38:30.159
We also encourage them
to send their children to school,

00:38:30.679 --> 00:38:32.439
as education is very important.

00:38:33.280 --> 00:38:35.040
We primarily raise awareness

00:38:35.919 --> 00:38:39.800
about the health hazards
of working in mica mines.

00:38:43.479 --> 00:38:46.760
Raul is 24 years old
and comes daily to the mines

00:38:46.840 --> 00:38:48.840
accompanied by these local campaigners.

00:38:49.479 --> 00:38:51.879
He goes to families
one by one to warn them.

00:38:55.959 --> 00:38:57.800
-Do you come and help sometimes?
-Yes.

00:39:01.560 --> 00:39:03.560
-Do you like going to school?
-Yes.

00:39:06.600 --> 00:39:09.719
Today, the group is going to focus
on the family's mother.

00:39:10.399 --> 00:39:14.560
They're asking her to stop her activity
and listen to their recommendations.

00:39:15.399 --> 00:39:19.000
After a short negotiation,
she agrees to take them to her home.

00:39:31.600 --> 00:39:32.639
On their way there,

00:39:33.280 --> 00:39:36.679
the group attempts to build
a friendly rapport with the miners.

00:39:46.879 --> 00:39:49.800
Panchia Devi lives here
with her four children.

00:39:50.120 --> 00:39:51.679
Her husband lives in Delhi.

00:39:52.199 --> 00:39:54.199
She has to take care of them on her own.

00:39:55.000 --> 00:39:57.000
Are you aware of the problems that you

00:39:57.080 --> 00:40:00.120
and your children
are facing when you go into the mines?

00:40:00.479 --> 00:40:02.080
No, I've been going since I was little,

00:40:02.159 --> 00:40:03.959
and my daughter
only helps from time to time.

00:40:04.040 --> 00:40:07.159
What you need to know
is that when you are sorting the mica,

00:40:07.239 --> 00:40:09.320
dust is released.

00:40:09.800 --> 00:40:13.080
As a result,
children risk catching tuberculosis

00:40:13.159 --> 00:40:15.239
and will also develop a cough.

00:40:15.600 --> 00:40:18.560
People working in the mines
or those who sort the mica

00:40:18.639 --> 00:40:20.760
are often diagnosed with tuberculosis.

00:40:21.560 --> 00:40:23.800
The dust enters the airways
and settles in the lungs.

00:40:23.879 --> 00:40:27.719
which prevents them
from functioning properly.

00:40:28.199 --> 00:40:33.760
When these airways are blocked,
it's difficult to breathe.

00:40:35.040 --> 00:40:38.199
The activist then makes
his strongest possible argument

00:40:38.320 --> 00:40:39.360
with the mother.

00:40:41.360 --> 00:40:44.520
Imagine if the authorities decided
to stop them mining for good,

00:40:44.600 --> 00:40:45.800
given that it's illegal.

00:40:46.399 --> 00:40:48.840
What would you do
if you no longer had work?

00:40:49.159 --> 00:40:53.280
I believe in God, He will help us.

00:40:53.360 --> 00:40:57.959
We don't have a choice here,
there's nothing else to do.

00:41:21.000 --> 00:41:24.399
The residents of Jharkhand
are trapped in a vicious cycle.

00:41:26.360 --> 00:41:29.600
They must choose between their health
or their survival.

00:41:34.280 --> 00:41:38.439
According to the NGO,
the only possible solution

00:41:38.800 --> 00:41:43.760
would be an aid plan for the development
of the region in order to create jobs.

00:41:46.439 --> 00:41:49.399
However, the local residents
are still waiting for this.

00:41:50.919 --> 00:41:52.800
How long will they have to wait?

